    "updated_at": "2020-02-26T09:42:16Z",
    "body": "Ok, I can confirm this happens on one of my machines as well. Here it looks like the issue is that the status is coming from a prior `PROMPT_COMMAND`, not from the command that was run. After clearing that so that only the `starship` command is run it works fine:\r\n\r\n```console\r\n> echo $PROMPT_COMMAND\r\nprintf \"\\033_%s@%s:%s\\033\\\\\" \"${USER}\" \"${HOSTNAME%%.*}\" \"${PWD/#$HOME/\\~}\";starship_precmd;\r\n> PROMPT_COMMAND=starship_precmd\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat `PROMPT_COMMAND` seems to be coming from the default Arch system `/etc/bash.bashrc` for a bunch of terminal emulators.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
