    "updated_at": "2020-02-26T10:03:46Z",
    "body": "Yes, it seems like a bug in the starship init script. It can't use `$?` in the `precmd` to get the command status if the user has any other `PROMPT_COMMAND`s configured, but I have no idea what it can use instead. (Or maybe this is a bug in `bash` since it says \"`$?` Expands to the exit status of the most recently executed *foreground pipeline*\" and the other prompt commands shouldn't be considered a foreground pipeline?).\r\n\r\nIt looks like using https://github.com/rcaloras/bash-preexec at least fixes it, it stores `$?` and resets it before invoking each `precmd` function.",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
